  "findings": [
    "The empty callbacks are proven semantically redundant, and all 11 changed default mappers pass enabled-architecture normal/DIET validation.",
    "Removing the call improves several raw panels, but 18 panels regress more than one percent; affected outputs include Clang ARM formatting/detail, MIPS and AArch64 detail, and GCC PE32 detail.",
    "All three x86-host compiler profiles add instructions to PE32/PE64 detail. The generic null test is therefore not cost-free for required x86 mappers. This explains a source-level added cost but does not by itself fully attribute every native regression."
  ],
  "decision": "Hold; do not publish the nullable mapper prototype. Keep the proof and native negative results. Any next version must preserve the required-mapper path and account for the non-x86 detail regressions.",
